      "summary_sent_score": 0.35252100229263306
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 10,
      "text": "3. Learned counsel for the State submits that the statement of the victim has been recorded under Section 164 of Cr.P.C.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 732,
      "end": 852,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Section 164",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 830,
          "end": 841
        },
        {
          "text": "Cr.P.C.",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 845,
          "end": 852
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.18392102420330048
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 11,
      "text": "In her statement, she inter alia stated that without informing her family members, she left the house and proceeded to Gunupur.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 853,
      "end": 980,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Gunupur",
          "label": "GPE",
          "start": 972,
          "end": 979
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.17515723407268524
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 12,
      "text": "When she was trying to get an accommodation, she took the help of the present petitioner, who is an auto driver.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 981,
      "end": 1093,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.23343221843242645
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 13,
      "text": "The // 2 //\npetitioner took her to a hotel, but no room was vacant there.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 1094,
      "end": 1167,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.2145281434059143
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 14,
      "text": "Then the petitioner suggested the victim to accompany him to a place to stay there with him.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 1168,
      "end": 1260,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.22650575637817383
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 15,
      "text": "While the victim was taking rest, the petitioner tried to ravish her.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 1261,
      "end": 1330,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.300852507352829
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 16,
      "text": "But the victim some how escaped from his clutches.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 1331,
      "end": 1381,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.19320659339427948
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 17,
      "text": "Then the petitioner dropped the victim near the railway station.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 1382,
      "end": 1446,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.30910226702690125
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 18,
      "text": "4. In view of the aforementioned, I am not inclined to entertain this application at this stage.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RPC",
      "start": 1448,
      "end": 1544,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.06178940832614899
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 19,
      "text": "However, the petitioner is granted liberty to renew his prayer for bail after examination of the victim.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RPC",
      "start": 1545,
      "end": 1650,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.3046332001686096
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 20,
      "text": "It is expected that the learned trial Court would see to it that the victim is preferentially examined before the formal witnesses.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 1651,
      "end": 1782,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 21,
      "text": "The petitioner may renew his bail plea after expiry of three months, if the trial is not proceeded at the expected pace.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RPC",
      "start": 1783,
      "end": 1903,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.24202807247638702
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 22,
      "text": "5. With this observation, the BLAPL stands disposed of.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 1905,
      "end": 1960,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false
    },
